{{also|Tiede|tiède}}
==Finnish==

===Etymology===
{{suf|fi|tietää|t1=to know|e}}. {{coin|fi|w=fi:|Wolmar Schildt|nat=Finnish|occ=physician and translator|in=1842}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-p|tieDe*}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[science]] {{gloss|collective discipline of learning, including the [[liberal arts]] or [[humanities]]}}

====Usage notes====
* {{m|fi||tiede}} in the singular is either a generic term or refers to a particular discipline; the plural {{m|fi|tieteet}} may be used collectively of the sciences, including the liberal arts and humanities.
* Unlike {{m+|en|science}} in current usage, this term includes more than just the [[natural science]]s. If one wants to refer to them in particular, {{m|fi|luonnontiede}} can be used.

